Batocera Games Catalog - Debian Package

INSTALLATION:
=============
1. Install the package:
   sudo dpkg -i batocera-games-catalog_1.0.0_all.deb
   sudo apt-get install -f  # Install missing dependencies if needed

2. Configure the backend:
   sudo nano /opt/batocera-games-catalog/backend/.env
   
   Required settings:
   - DISCORD_CLIENT_ID
   - DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET
   - DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN
   - DISCORD_GUILD_ID
   - GAMES_PATH
   - DATABASE_URL
   - SECRET_KEY

3. Start the services:
   sudo systemctl start batocera-games-catalog-backend
   sudo systemctl start batocera-games-catalog-frontend

4. Enable services to start on boot:
   sudo systemctl enable batocera-games-catalog-backend
   sudo systemctl enable batocera-games-catalog-frontend

SERVICES:
=========
- Backend API: http://localhost:8000
- Frontend: http://localhost:3000

MANAGEMENT:
===========
Check status:
  sudo systemctl status batocera-games-catalog-backend
  sudo systemctl status batocera-games-catalog-frontend

View logs:
  sudo journalctl -u batocera-games-catalog-backend -f
  sudo journalctl -u batocera-games-catalog-frontend -f

Restart services:
  sudo systemctl restart batocera-games-catalog-backend
  sudo systemctl restart batocera-games-catalog-frontend

NGINX & SSL SETUP:
==================
1. Install nginx and certbot (if not already installed):
   sudo apt-get install nginx certbot python3-certbot-nginx

2. Enable nginx site:
   sudo ln -s /etc/nginx/sites-available/batocera-games-catalog /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/
   sudo nginx -t
   sudo systemctl reload nginx

3. Setup SSL certificate with Let's Encrypt:
   sudo /opt/batocera-games-catalog/scripts/setup-ssl.sh your-domain.com your-email@example.com

   This will:
   - Update nginx config with your domain
   - Obtain SSL certificate from Let's Encrypt
   - Configure automatic renewal
   - Redirect HTTP to HTTPS

4. Update domain in nginx config (if needed):
   sudo /opt/batocera-games-catalog/scripts/update-nginx-domain.sh your-domain.com

5. Test certificate renewal:
   sudo certbot renew --dry-run

UNINSTALLATION:
===============
  sudo systemctl stop batocera-games-catalog-backend
  sudo systemctl stop batocera-games-catalog-frontend
  sudo dpkg -r batocera-games-catalog

FILES:
======
Installation directory: /opt/batocera-games-catalog/
Configuration: /opt/batocera-games-catalog/backend/.env
Logs: /opt/batocera-games-catalog/logs/
Data: /opt/batocera-games-catalog/data/

